# Test-only relaxations of the root .clang-tidy (everything else is inherited). Each plugin's
# tests/.clang-tidy is a copy of this file: clang-tidy reads the nearest .clang-tidy above the
# translation unit, and plugins/<id>/tests/ does not sit below this directory.
#
# - bugprone-unchecked-optional-access: doctest's REQUIRE(x.has_value()) is a do/while that logs
#   and does not return in the check's flow model, so every guarded x-> afterwards is reported.
# - clang-analyzer-optin.core.EnumCastOutOfRange: tests cast out-of-range integers on purpose to
#   reach the default branch of every enum switch (ErrorCode 255, avifResult 999), and the check
#   also fires inside the MSVC STL (<filesystem> bitmask enums) when a test calls file_size().
# - bugprone-random-generator-seed (clang-tidy 22, the CI runner's version): a constant seed is the
#   point of the hostile corpus and its self-tests - the same mutants on every run and every
#   machine, so a finding is reproducible (tests/support/HostileCorpusTests.cpp seeds 42 and 7,
#   the corpus itself 20260912).
# - bugprone-bitwise-pointer-cast (clang-tidy 22): the e2e host driver turns GetProcAddress's FARPROC
#   into the SDK's export signatures with std::bit_cast (tests/e2e/PluginHost.cpp), the host's own
#   idiom; every other spelling is refused by something else - a direct reinterpret_cast by clang's
#   -Wcast-function-type-mismatch (/WX), a void* intermediate by bugprone-casting-through-void, an
#   integer intermediate by performance-no-int-to-ptr, memcpy by this very check.
---
InheritParentConfig: true
Checks: >
  -bugprone-unchecked-optional-access,
  -clang-analyzer-optin.core.EnumCastOutOfRange,
  -bugprone-random-generator-seed,
  -bugprone-bitwise-pointer-cast
...
